:"fast","#text":"Biographies"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"AMACOM","dateIssued":["c1999",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1999"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xiii, 162 p. ; 23 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"Business the Jack Welch Way takes you behind the scenes to trace the remarkable career - and uncover the successful business strategies - of the man who's often called the most powerful CEO in America. What does he most value? How does he compare running gigantic GE to operating a corner grocery store? And how did the most acclaimed S.O.B. of the eighties transform himself into a role model of 21st-century management?\" \"You'll learn the answers to these questions (and plenty more) as this fast, fun, and enlightening book unfolds the ten key secrets of this incredible turnaround king.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"tableOfContents":"The Life and Times of Jack Welch 1 -- 1 Invest in People 23 -- 2 Dominate Your Market ... or Get Out 35 -- 3 Never Sit Still 43 -- 4 Think Service 61 -- 5 Forget the Past; Love the Future 73 -- 6 Learn and Lead 87 -- 7 No Bull 103 -- 8 Kill Bureaucracy 115 -- 9 Stick Around 127 -- 10 Manage the Corner Store 141 -- How Long Can Jack Welch Be Effective? 149 -- How to Manage the Jack Welch Way 153.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Stuart Crainer."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Welch, Jack (John Francis)",{"